s coercing an unknown type to Task via the LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA lookup and prescribes an identical 'resolve via effective type map / raise fail-closed' fix, but adapters/jira/acli.py:282 does NOT use LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA — it computes issue_type = ticket_data.get('ticket_type','Task').capitalize(), a passthrough capitalize with no map lookup and no LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA import. An unknown syncable type (e.g. 'spike') is NOT coerced to Task there; it is passed through capitalized. The edit target exists, but the uniform framing understates that acli.py needs a materially different rewrite (introduce the map lookup + fail-closed) than the other two paths.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22f0b0326cd957a6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'Remove silent type-coerce default at the three create paths ... adapters/jira/acli.py:282'; Approach outcome 3 (FAIL-CLOSED)","norm_id":"n124c9f6dca4a782e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer applies the same map-swap+fail-closed edit to acli.py as to the other two paths and finds no _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE lookup to replace, or misses that acli currently passes unknown types through capitalized rather than coercing to Task"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Scope, split the acli.py bullet from the other two: note acli.py currently does `ticket_data.get('ticket_type','Task').capitalize()` (no map), so the edit must add effective-type-map resolution + fail-closed raise, replacing the capitalize passthrough.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the source of the Jira->local reverse TYPE map used by _desired_type_annotation's lossy check (mirror config.jira_to_local_status): add a config-level reverse type map so outbound_labels stays config-only, rather than inverting the collapsed forward map or importing inbound_fields/value_maps.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '_desired_type_annotation (mirror _desired_status_annotation) ... stamp only when the forward map is LOSSY (target does not reverse to this local type)'","outbound_labels.py:105-110 _desired_status_annotation reverses via config.jira_to_local_status","config.py has NO reverse type map (only jira_to_local_status/local_to_jira_status)","inbound_fields.py:105 _JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE is the only Jira->local type reverse literal, and it is in a DIFFERENT module outbound_labels does not import","outbound_labels.py:19 imports only `config`"],"finding":"The lossy-stamp rule for _desired_type_annotation (\"stamp only when target does not reverse to this local type\") requires a Jira->local reverse TYPE map at the outbound_labels layer, but the plan never identifies its source; config.py has no reverse type map (unlike config.jira_to_local_status), the reverse map lives only in inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE, and outbound_labels.py deliberately imports only `config`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b42ebd4df81a8be","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / New symbols: outbound_labels._desired_type_annotation","norm_id":"nc04aff0280da0ac9","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a config.jira_to_local_type built-in reverse map (parity-tested against inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE, mirroring config.jira_to_local_status <-> inbound_differ._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS) and have _desired_type_annotation consult it.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the port/signature change that threads the effective per-project type map into the create mappers (extend OutboundMapper.map_local_to_remote at _backend.py:372 with a type_map param, mirroring S2's status_map, and resolve it via an _effective_type_map_for analog at the builder sites) so fail-closed resolution has the map it checks against.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["outbound_fields.py:143 and jira_datacenter/backend.py:86 build issuetype from a locally-imported _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE, not a passed-in map","_backend.py:372 map_local_to_remote port carries status_map (S2) but no type_map","outbound_mutation_builders.py:80-93 threads status_map into map_local_to_remote; the plan's Finding 1 threads only the type STAMP diff, not a type map into the mapper","Plan Scope lists the three create sites but names no port/signature change"],"finding":"Fail-closed resolution at the create mappers requires the effective per-project TYPE map to reach outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields and jira_datacenter/backend, but the plan does not extend the map_local_to_remote Backend port (_backend.py:372) / mapper signatures to carry a type_map, the way S2 added status_map.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f48eb5a32f3fb4f5a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'resolve via effective type map; raise fail-closed on an unmapped syncable type'","norm_id":"n7b3f90632c6af97f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how acli.py:283's create_issue (which uses .capitalize() and receives no map/project key) obtains the effective type map and fails closed, since it is not on the map_local_to_remote port path that the other two create sites use.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["acli.py:282 issue_type = ticket_data.get('ticket_type','Task').capitalize() — no _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE, no status_map/project seam","outbound_fields.py:143 and jira_datacenter/backend.py:86 both use _LOCAL_TO_JIRA_TYPE.get(...,'Task') and receive status_map","map_local_to_remote port defined at _backend.py:372, jira/backend.py:73, jira_datacenter/backend.py:121 — acli.create_issue is not one of these"],"finding":"The third create path acli.py:282 is structurally unlike the other two: it derives issuetype via ticket_data.get('ticket_type','Task').capitalize() with NO map lookup and is the transport's own create_issue rather than the OutboundMapper port the other two flow through, yet the plan treats all three uniformly.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c4a7fab606d841c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: three create paths — adapters/jira/acli.py:282","norm_id":"n41f9124ef6ba6dda","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.85,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a config-load fail-closed step (per parent AC 'fails closed at config load'): feed the universe of syncable local types (get_args(TicketType) − EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES) into a load-time validation that raises when any non-skipped syncable type has no target in the effective type map — do not rely on the three create-path raises alone.","cohort":["G7"],"criteria":["G7"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Parent 3d7a AC: 'an unmapped-non-skipped type **fails closed at config load** — verified per child.'","Parent 3d7a child decomposition: 'S3 ... delivers the no-analogue-type answers and **load-time fail-closed on undecided types**.'","Leaf approach #3: 'an unmapped, non-skipped syncable type **raises rather than coercing**' with AC `test_unmapped_syncable_type_fails_closed` — 'unmapped non-skipped syncable type raises (no Task coercion) **across the three create paths**.'","Leaf Scope: '... resolve via effective type map; raise fail-closed on an unmapped syncable type' listed only under the three create-path files — no config-load validation step.","S1 mapping_config.validate (mapping_config.py:328-359) only checks axis-map values against declared vocab; it has no knowledge of the universe of local rebar types, so it cannot catch an undecided local type at load without an added check — consistent with the leaf's own round-1 review comment B5.","Config-load fail-closed catches an undecided type eagerly regardless of whether such a ticket exists; create-path fail-closed fires only lazily when a ticket of that type is created — the parent's goal of load-time detection does not hold under the leaf's plan."],"finding":"The leaf relocates the parent's 'fails closed at config load' deliverable to fail-closed only at the three outbound create paths (application time), contradicting the parent AC and the S3 decomposition line ('load-time fail-closed on undecided types').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1b7b419c0a0cf9c0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach outcome #3 (FAIL-CLOSED) and AC line `test_unmapped_syncable_type_fails_closed`","norm_id":"nc624586bb83ff9c4","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A project declares a type_map that omits a syncable local type (e.g. 'bug') and does not SKIP it: the parent wants this rejected at config load (rebar doctor / load), but the leaf as planned would accept the config and only raise later when a bug ticket happens to reach a create path — possibly never surfacing in a project with no open bugs.","An operator validating config before any sync run gets no error under the leaf plan, contradicting the parent's load-time guarantee."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Keep the create-path raises as a defense-in-depth backstop, but add a load-time check (invoked where effective_type_map/effective_excluded_sync_types resolve, mirroring how doctor/load validate config) that asserts every syncable local type either maps to a target or is skipped, raising MappingConfigError at load. Add an AC asserting the load-time raise (not only the create-path raise).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add apply_inbound_events.py:75-76 (inbound-CREATE channel, `_JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, \"task\")`) to the inbound recover_type_label scope, mirroring how recover_status_label is applied at BOTH inbound_fields.py:328 and apply_inbound_events.py:156.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'inbound_fields.recover_type_label (mirror recover_status_label inbound_fields.py:152) ... applied at the inbound issuetype site inbound_fields.py:311-313 with the same \"prefer label over raw\" order as recover_status_label at inbound_fields.py:326'","recover_status_label is applied at TWO sites: inbound_fields.py:328 and apply_inbound_events.py:156 (grep of recover_status_label)","Omitted site: apply_inbound_events.py:75-76 `issuetype = _extract_name(fields.get(\"issuetype\"), \"Task\"); ticket_type = _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, \"task\")` — the inbound-CREATE-channel type resolution, symmetric with the status STATUS-event recovery the plan mirrors"],"finding":"The inbound-recovery scope for the new recover_type_label omits a second inbound issuetype->ticket_type resolution site. The plan names only inbound_fields.py:311-313, but issuetype->ticket_type is ALSO resolved at apply_inbound_events.py:75-76 (`ticket_type = _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, \"task\")`) in the inbound-CREATE channel. This is the exact type-analog of the status path the plan says it mirrors: recover_status_label is applied at BOTH inbound_fields.py:328 AND apply_inbound_events.py:156. Patching only one inbound site breaks the round-trip symmetry the plan claims.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2f48b101a16dc762","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope: `inbound_fields.recover_type_label ... applied at the inbound issuetype site inbound_fields.py:311-313`","norm_id":"n95e604baef28865e","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["apply_inbound_events.py:75-76 (inbound-CREATE channel) is not in Scope: recover_type_label is never threaded there, so a Jira-originated CREATE carrying a rebar-type: label does not recover its original local type — the round-trip is lossy exactly where the plan claims symmetry, and test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free may pass against inbound_fields only while apply_inbound_events silently regresses."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Scope, extend the inbound-recovery item to both inbound issuetype sites: inbound_fields.py:311-313 AND apply_inbound_events.py:75-76; thread recover_type_label with the same 'prefer label over raw' precedence at each, and cover both in test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the fail-closed raise names the offending local type and project key, and state whether an unmapped type aborts the whole outbound batch or is surfaced per-ticket (partial-state/blast-radius behavior).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.548,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'FAIL-CLOSED — an unmapped, non-skipped syncable type raises rather than coercing.'","'resolve per project key inside the loop, since a batch can span projects' — the per-ticket loop at outbound_differ.py:430 means a raise there is a new failure point in a batch context","Plan does not state the error message contents or whether the raise aborts the whole batch vs. surfaces per-ticket"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new fail-closed raise for unmapped syncable types but does not specify that the raised error is diagnostic (naming the offending local type and project key) nor how a mid-batch raise interacts with partial batch progress — a single unmapped type could abort processing of the remaining tickets in a multi-project batch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2007372610354de9","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach outcome 3 'FAIL-CLOSED'; Scope 'raise fail-closed on an unmapped syncable type'","norm_id":"n7aaf3848bd720451","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an AC asserting the raised exception message includes the local type and project key, and document the intended batch behavior (fail-fast whole-batch vs. skip-and-collect) at the outbound_differ.py:430 loop site.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Qualify the TicketType citation as `rebar.types.TicketType` (src/rebar/types.py:23) to distinguish it from the reconciler-relative paths used elsewhere in the plan.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.315,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/types.py:23: TicketType = Literal[...]","search for TicketType under src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler returned (no matches)","line 23 and content match, but the module is rebar.types, not a reconciler-local types.py"],"finding":"The plan cites `get_args(TicketType)` (`types.py:23`) using a reconciler-relative path style, but TicketType lives at src/rebar/types.py:23 (module rebar.types), not at src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/types.py — there is no types.py in the reconciler package. Every other file citation in the plan is reconciler-relative, so this one is inconsistent and could send an implementer to the wrong module.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5212546542b4ea16","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (Syncable derivation) and Scope: 'get_args(TicketType) (types.py:23)'","norm_id":"n4c7a96fb693298a8","priority":0.385,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer looks for types.py inside the reconciler package to derive _LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB and cannot find it"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change `get_args(TicketType) (types.py:23)` to `get_args(TicketType) (rebar.types.TicketType, src/rebar/types.py:23)`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge that removing silent Task-coercion is a behavior break for previously-coerced unmapped syncable types, and state the back-out/expand-contract path (e.g. the built-in map default preserves current behavior for {bug,epic,story,task}, and unmapped types require an explicit type_map or skip entry before rollout).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.535,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'three create paths silently coercing an unknown type to Task'","'FAIL-CLOSED — an unmapped, non-skipped syncable type raises rather than coercing'","Default effective_type_map equals LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA (AC test_effective_type_map_default_equals_builtin), so built-in types are unaffected — the break is scoped to previously-coerced unmapped syncable types."],"finding":"Removing the silent Task-coercion default at the three create paths and replacing it with a fail-closed raise is a behavior change for any deployment currently relying on unmapped types being coerced to Task; the plan states the intent (FAIL-CLOSED) but does not acknowledge the break for existing consumers nor state a rollback / expand-contract path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ea62d4d55c1d5f1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: 'Remove silent type-coerce default at the three create paths ... raise fail-closed'","norm_id":"n2a29629e861dcafd","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An existing project syncing a syncable type that was silently coerced to Task now raises and blocks the sync run after this change ships."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a Compat note: the change is behavior-preserving for built-in types (default map == LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA); for any other syncable type an operator must add a type_map remap or a skip entry before this ships, and document that reverting the config restores the prior mapping.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confir